# ThreadSanitizer: one race in LVGL itself, not in lv_draw_ortho.
#
# LVGL 9.6 and master read a circle-cache entry's `life` in
# release_mask_radius() (src/draw/sw/lv_draw_sw_mask.c) outside
# circle_cache_mutex, while another thread's acquire_mask_radius_from_cache()
# ages the same entry under it. 9.5 reads it under the mutex. LVGL's own
# drawing threads (LV_DRAW_SW_DRAW_UNIT_CNT > 1) meet the same race. The read
# only asks whether `life` is negative, which a cached entry never is (it is
# set to 0 and only ever raised, up to 1000), so the answer cannot change.
race:release_mask_radius
